<title>JAPAN: TABLE - Tokyo July consumer prices up 1.4% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Tokyo July consumer prices up 1.4% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo area consumer prices rose 1.4 percent in July compared with a year earlier, while nationwide consumer prices increased 2.2 percent in June, the Management and Coordination Agency said on Friday.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of consumer prices in Tokyo and nationwide (index base 1995):</p>
<p>				   JUL	 JUNE	  MAY</p>
<p> Tokyo overall index     101.4	101.8	 101.8</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	  +1.4 pct   +1.8 pct    +1.4 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	-0.4 pct    0.0 pct    +0.3 pct</p>
<p> Tokyo core index	  101.5	101.7	 101.8</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	  +1.6 pct   +1.6 pct    +1.6 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	-0.2 pct   -0.1 pct    +0.3 pct</p>
<p>				  JUNE	 MAY	   APR</p>
<p> Nationwide overall index102.4	102.4	 102.2</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	  +2.2 pct   +1.9 pct    +1.9 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	 0.0 pct   +0.2 pct    +2.0 pct</p>
<p> Nationwide core index   102.3	102.4	 102.2</p>
<p>  yr-on-yr changes	  +2.0 pct   +2.1 pct    +2.0 pct</p>
<p>  mth-on-mth changes	-0.1 pct   +0.2 pct    +1.9 pct</p>
<p>(NOTE: The Tokyo index was calculated by collecting price data at mid-month. The core index, which is a key barometer for gauging core inflation, is overall prices minus fresh food prices. The base year is 1995.)</p>
</text>
